{start_of_verse: Verse 11}
Daniel Decatur Emmett  1859 *
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh, I [G]wish I was in the land of cotton,
[C]Old times there are not forgotten,
Look [G]away, look [Em]away, look [D]away Dixie [G]Land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
In [G]Dixie Land, where I was born in,
[C]early on one frosty mornin',
Look [G]away, look [Em]away, look [D]away Dixie [G]Land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I [G]wish I was in [C]Dixie, [A7]Hooray! [D]Hooray!
In [G]Dixie Land I'll [C]take my stand
to [G]live and die in [D]Dixie.
[G]Away, [D]away, [G]away down south in [D][G]Dixie.
[G]Away, [D]away, [G]away down south in [D][G]Dixie.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Ole [G]Missus marry "Will the weaver",
[C]Willum was a gay deceiver,
Look [G]away! Look [Em]away! Look [D]away!
Dixie [G]Land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
But [G]when he put his arm around 'er,
[C]He smiled fierce as a forty pounder,
Look [G]away! Look [Em]away! Look [D]away!
Dixie [G]Land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I [G]wish I was in [C]Dixie, [A7]Hooray! [D]Hooray!
In [G]Dixie Land I'll [C]take my stand
to [G]live and die in [D]Dixie.
[G]Away, [D]away, [G]away down south in [D][G]Dixie.
[G]Away, [D]away, [G]away down south in [D][G]Dixie.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
His [G]face was sharp as a butcher's cleaver,
[C]But that did not seem to grieve 'er,
Look [G]away! Look [Em]away! Look [D]away!
Dixie [G]Land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Ole [G]Missus acted the foolish part,
[C]And died for a man that broke her heart,
Look [G]away! Look [Em]away! Look [D]away!
Dixie [G]Land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I [G]wish I was in [C]Dixie, [A7]Hooray! [D]Hooray!
In [G]Dixie Land I'll [C]take my stand
to [G]live and die in [D]Dixie.
[G]Away, [D]away, [G]away down south in [D][G]Dixie.
[G]Away, [D]away, [G]away down south in [D][G]Dixie.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
Now [G]here's a health to the next ole Missus,
[C]An' all the gals that want to kiss us,
Look [G]away! Look [Em]away! Look [D]away!
Dixie [G]Land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
But [G]if you want to drive 'way sorrow,
[C]Come and hear this song tomorrow,
Look [G]away! Look [Em]away! Look [D]away!
Dixie [G]Land.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I [G]wish I was in [C]Dixie, [A7]Hooray! [D]Hooray!
In [G]Dixie Land I'll [C]take my stand
to [G]live and die in [D]Dixie.
